# The coverage page is generated and checked in, which is deliberate: a
# status change shows up in review rather than nowhere. Two branches that
# each flip a status render two different pages, and a table cell is not an
# edit git can reconcile.
#
# The page is a function of committed files, so the resolution is mechanical:
# keep either copy, then `make coverage-page` regenerates it from the merged
# status files and registries with no test report. Configure the driver once
# with `make setup-dev`, or directly:
#
#     git config merge.coverage-generated.driver true
#
# Without that config git falls back to a normal merge and conflicts, so a
# fresh clone is never worse off than it is today.
#
# The status files under docs/coverage/status carry no driver on purpose. One
# row per line is what lets git merge them, and "keep ours" would discard a
# status flip from main that only CI could restore.
docs/coverage/matrix.md merge=coverage-generated
